<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 3</span></div>
	
			<h2>Combine the backbone and base</h2>
	
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<ol>
<li>Bolt the T-bar. which is the backbone of the bot, to the blueboards. One hole should be on the right blueboard and the rest should be on the left blueboard.</li>
</ol>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="992" height="872" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-BackboneBase-992x872.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="Viking Ship Bot Backbone&amp;Base" title="Viking Ship Bot Backbone&amp;Base" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-BackboneBase.png 992w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-BackboneBase-300x264.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 992px) 100vw, 992px" /></div>
