		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a22165637173" name="6a22165637173" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 5</span></div>
	
			<h2>Connect the battery box</h2>
	
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<ol>
<li>Bolt the battery box to the short L-frames on the blueboard. The wires should be at the top of the battery box.</li>
<li>Attach two short standoffs to the fifth row of the blueboards. One standoff should be in the fifth column of the left blueboard and the other should be in the second row of the right blueboard.</li>
</ol>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="688" height="991" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-Battery-Box-688x991.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="Viking Ship Bot Battery Box" title="Viking Ship Bot Battery Box" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-Battery-Box.png 688w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-Battery-Box-208x300.png 208w" sizes="(max-width: 688px) 100vw, 688px" /></div>
