	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a221656384b2" name="6a221656384b2" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 6</span></div>
	
			<h2>Connect the Smart Inventor Board</h2>
	
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<ol>
<li>Bolt the Smart Inventor Board to the short standoffs on the blueboard. Pay attention to the Smart Inventor Board&#8217;s placement!</li>
</ol>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="688" height="991" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-Smart-Inventor-Board-688x991.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="Viking Ship Bot Smart Inventor Board" title="Viking Ship Bot Smart Inventor Board" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-Smart-Inventor-Board.png 688w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Bot-Smart-Inventor-Board-208x300.png 208w" sizes="(max-width: 688px) 100vw, 688px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a221656392cf" name="6a221656392cf" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 7</span></div>
	
			<h2>Build the Viking ship deck</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>For this entire step, pay attention to the orientation of the blueboards and placement of the parts!</p>
<ol>
<li>On the second column, attach long standoffs in the holes in the first and last rows.</li>
<li>Make a trapezoid with three 4-hole metal frames and one 7-hole metal frame, and then bolt the longest edge to the long standoffs.</li>
<li>On the last column, bolt a short standoff to each corner.</li>
<li>Bolt a 7-hole metal frame to the short standoffs.</li>
<li>Repeat steps 1-4 on another blueboard and then rotate so the two blueboards are mirror images of each other.</li>
</ol>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="992" height="464" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Deck-992x464.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="Viking Ship Deck" title="Viking Ship Deck" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Deck.png 992w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Viking-Ship-Deck-300x140.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 992px) 100vw, 992px" /></div>
